The candidate heading 8471 covers both complete automatic data processing (ADP) machines and “units thereof”. The specific classification emphasis defines a “unit of ADP machine” as an electronic device that is (i) electrical/electronic, (ii) used solely or principally with an ADP system, (iii) connectable to that system, and (iv) capable of exchanging data.  

The item description identifies the product as a “Dell 2.5 \" 480 GB 6G RI SATA SSD”. By industry knowledge, an SSD:
* Is an electronic storage device (electrical/electronic);
* Is designed exclusively for insertion into computers, servers, laptops, or similar ADP machines;
* Connects through a SATA interface, providing a physical link to the host;
* Stores and transfers digital data to/from the host computer, thereby exchanging data.

Therefore the SSD fulfills all four criteria and is unequivocally a “unit of an ADP machine”.

Requirement 2 (“Must not be elsewhere specified or included”) is satisfied because SSDs are not allocated to any other heading such as 8523 (record carriers) or 8541 (semiconductor devices). In the HS nomenclature they are normally placed under 8471.70 “Storage units”, confirming they are not “elsewhere specified”.

There are no listed exclusions that would apply to the SSD.

Since the category description aligns with the nature of the item, all requirements are definitively met, no exclusions apply, and the item is definitely the type described, the classification result is a MATCH.
